{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>He transferred.</b> A word that goes out on account of [something] being removed from one and given to another; like it: 'and the people he transferred' (Genesis 13:5). And Mordecai ruled over the house of Haman, for he had great wealth, also male and female slaves, for there was none greater than him after the king. And the sense of 'Esther added' is because her entire request was to destroy Haman."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "Genesis citation inferred from the quoted phrase 'ואת העם העביר אותו' in the Hebrew, though the wording does not exactly match the Masoretic text of Genesis 13:5."}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:14.837509343Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}